{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L193-L217","doc":"**Proposition** ([`prop:observation-energy`]) — resolving\ndeclaration for the `lean.ref` URI\n`qou:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy`.\n\nConjoins the three claims: (i) the quantum Planck constant strictly\nincreases, `ℏ_{q+δq} - ℏ_q = δq/(q(q+δq)) > 0` (derived sorry-free);\n(ii) the action deforms as `𝔖_{q+δq} = 𝔖_q + δq·∂𝔖_q/∂q + R₂(δq)`\nwith `R₂ = O(δq²)` (equation derived; the quadratic bound carries\nthe one honest `sorry`, see\n`observation_energy_remainder_quadratic`); (iii) the classical\nenergy is unconstrained in sign (derived from the witnesses). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:observation-energy","label":"prop:observation-energy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/observation-energy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_classical_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_classical_sign","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L183-L191","doc":"**Claim (iii) — derived from the sign witnesses.**  The classical\nenergy is unconstrained in sign under observation: there exist\nsubstrate points where it strictly increases and where it strictly\ndecreases (∃-packaging of the witness fields `q_inc` / `q_dec`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_remainder_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_remainder_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L134-L181","doc":"**Claim (ii), quadratic remainder — derived (conditional on `C^{1,1}`\nregularity).**  The Taylor remainder of the categorical action is `O(δ²)`\non the perturbation window: `∃ C, ∀ |δ| ≤ δq, |R₂(δ)| ≤ C·δ²`.  This is the\nsubstantive analytic content of the manuscript's\n`𝔖_{q'} = 𝔖_q + δq·∂𝔖_q/∂q + O((δq)²)`, now **proved** from the second-order\nregularity carried by `ObservationEnergyContext` (`S_hasDeriv` +\n`S'_lipschitz`: `S` is `C^{1,1}` with `dS_dq = S' q`) via the mean-value\ninequality — `C = L` works, since the remainder's derivative\n`S'(q+t) − dS_dq` is bounded by `L·|t| ≤ L·|δ|` on the segment, so\n`|R₂(δ)| ≤ L·|δ|·|δ| = L·δ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_action_deformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_action_deformation","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L124-L132","doc":"**Claim (ii), deformation equation — derived sorry-free.**\n`𝔖_{q+δq} = 𝔖_q + δq·∂𝔖_q/∂q + R₂(δq)`, a rearrangement of the\ndefining equation `R_2_def` for the remainder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_hbar_diff_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_hbar_diff_pos","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L114-L122","doc":"**Claim (i), positivity — derived sorry-free.**  The quantum-energy\nshift `δq / (q(q+δq))` is strictly positive for `δq > 0`, `q > 1`:\nevery observation with positive substrate perturbation strictly\nincreases the quantum energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_hbar_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.observation_energy_hbar_diff","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**Claim (i), difference identity — derived sorry-free.**\n`ℏ_{q+δq} - ℏ_q = δq / (q(q+δq))`, from the defining equation\n`ℏ_x = 1 - x⁻¹` by clearing denominators (`q, q+δq ≠ 0` from the\npositivity hypotheses). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S'_lipschitz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S'_lipschitz","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L99-L99","doc":"**Second-order regularity of the action** (the `C^{1,1}` input the\n`O(δ²)` remainder needs): `S'` is `L`-Lipschitz measured from `q` on the\nwindow. At `x = q` this forces `S' q = dS_dq`; away from `q` it bounds how\nfast the slope may change. This is the honest analytic hypothesis the\nmanuscript's `O((δq)²)` claim rests on — an input, not the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.L_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.L_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The regularity constant is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.L","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.L","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Second-order regularity constant (a Lipschitz bound on `S'`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S_hasDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S_hasDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The action `S` is differentiable everywhere with derivative `S'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S'","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Derivative function `S' = ∂𝔖/∂q` of the categorical action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.E_dec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.E_dec","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The classical energy decreases at `q_dec`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.E_inc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.E_inc","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The classical energy increases at `q_inc`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q_dec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q_dec","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Witness point where the classical energy decreases under the\nperturbation (sign-witness data for claim (iii)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q_inc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q_inc","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Witness point where the classical energy increases under the\nperturbation (sign-witness data for claim (iii)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.E_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.E_classical","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Classical energy `q ↦ E_classical(q)` (the `q → 1` shadow of the\naction), opaque model data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.R_2_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.R_2_def","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Defining equation: `R₂(δ)` *is* the first-order Taylor remainder\nof the action at `q` (definitional input, not a conclusion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.R_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.R_2","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Second-order remainder `R₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.dS_dq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.dS_dq","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L67-L67","doc":"First-order observation cost `∂𝔖_q/∂q`, opaque model data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.S","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Categorical action `q ↦ 𝔖_q` ([`def:categorical-action`]),\nopaque model data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.hbar_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.hbar_eq","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Defining equation `ℏ_x = 1 - x⁻¹`\n([`def:quantum-planck-constant`]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.hbar","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Quantum Planck constant as a function of the substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.δq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.δq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The perturbation is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.δq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.δq","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Substrate perturbation `δq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Substrate regime `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.q","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ObservationEnergyContext","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/observation_energy.lean#L45-L99","doc":"Model data for [`prop:observation-energy`].  All fields are *inputs*\n(defining equations, positivity hypotheses, opaque model data,\nsign-witness points); none carries a conclusion of the\nproposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}